# Supabase and backend

## Authority

- PostgreSQL + typed contracts are the source of truth.
- Enforce input, authz, and business rules server-side.
- Recalculate/verify prices, availability, capacity, referrals, vouchers, permissions, and payment state on the server.
- Never trust browser-submitted totals or workflow state.
- Never disable RLS or expose service-role / privileged keys to the client.

## Clients

- `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` — cookie-aware user-scoped client; never reads service key.
- `src/lib/supabase/admin.ts` — server-only privileged client; call explicitly only when required.
- Repositories live in `src/server/repositories`; validate with Zod; map to view models.

## Schema changes

- Use migrations under `supabase/migrations`.
- Keep generated types in sync (`src/types/database.ts`).
- Do not hand-copy row shapes across files; derive from generated types or Zod RPC schemas.

## Storage

- Validate type, size, ownership, and authorization before upload.
- Keep Storage objects and DB metadata synchronized.
- Never invent bucket names or policies; inspect existing ones first.
